              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for to come out, then the French for the publication."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: le journal télévisé",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le journal télévisé — \"the television news\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nous regardons le journal télévisé à vingt heures. We watch the television news at eight in the evening."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often le JT in speech, or le journal de vingt heures."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "journal is inherited from Latin diurnālis \"daily\" (EtymDB); télévisé is built on télévision, from Greek tēle \"far\" and Latin vīsiō \"sight\", from vidēre \"to see\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
